1057	## 9. Functional requirements and acceptance criteria
1058	
1059	Every acceptance criterion (AC) should be checkable by a test or by a scripted manual step in §14.
1060	
1061	### F1. Authentication and onboarding (P0), owned by B (P0 wires the auth itself)
1062	
1063	**Requirements.** Use `@auth0/nextjs-auth0` v4 with `src/lib/auth0.ts` exporting `new Auth0Client()`. `src/proxy.ts` returns `auth0.middleware(request)` with the documented matcher that excludes `_next/static`, `_next/image`, `favicon.ico`, `sitemap.xml` and `robots.txt` ([Auth0 blog](https://auth0.com/blog/handling-auth-nextjs16-with-server-actions-middleware/)). The SDK mounts `/auth/login`, `/auth/logout`, `/auth/callback`, `/auth/profile` and `/auth/access-token` ([README](https://github.com/auth0/nextjs-auth0)). `requireUser()` in `src/lib/current-user.ts` calls `auth0.getSession()`, upserts `users` by `sub`, and returns `{ id, sub, tz, diets, allergens }`. **Every route handler and Server Action calls it.** Server Actions "must re-validate authentication explicitly", and `useUser()` is for UI only ([Auth0 blog](https://auth0.com/blog/handling-auth-nextjs16-with-server-actions-middleware/)). Do not merge users by email: social and password logins produce different `sub` values, and the free plan has no account linking (research inference from [Auth0 pricing](https://auth0.com/pricing)). Enable Google social login in the Auth0 dashboard.
1064	
1065	**AC**
1066	1. A logged-out visit to `/today` redirects to `/auth/login`. `GET /api/pantry` without a session returns 401 JSON.
1067	2. After first login a `users` row exists with `auth0_sub = session.user.sub`. A second login does not create a duplicate.
1068	3. With two test accounts, user A's `GET /api/pantry` never returns user B's items, and `PATCH /api/pantry/<B's id>` as A returns 404.
1069	4. `/onboarding` saves diets, allergens, goals and tz. `onboarded_at` is set, and later visits skip onboarding.

